[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69435,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cystic partially differentiated nephroblastoma (CPDN) is a multilocular, exclusively cystic renal neoplasm of very young children, containing nephroblastomatous tissue.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69436,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8959/1 Cystic partially differentiated nephroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69437,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C90.Y &amp; XH1JB4 Other specified malignant neoplasms of kidney, except renal pelvis &amp; Cystic partially differentiated nephroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69438,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69439,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69440,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CPDN arises in the kidney. There are exceptionally rare cases of bilateral CPDN {26850814; 25878237}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69441,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The typical presentation is that of an abdominal mass. The purely cystic nature of the lesion may be evident on imaging studies.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69442,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>More than 100&nbsp;patients with CPDN have been reported in the literature, with a male predominance. Patients usually present before the age of 2&nbsp;years {33673661}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69443,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CPDN is considered part of the nephroblastoma spectrum. Paediatric cystic nephroma used to be considered related to CPDN, but recent genetic studies have shown that cystic nephroma harbours <em>DICER1</em> mutations whereas CPDN does not, indicating that these two morphologically similar lesions are unrelated {24481001}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69444,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69445,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CPDNs often are large (particularly considering the patients&rsquo; young age), reaching diameters as great as 190&nbsp;mm (mean: 100&nbsp;mm). They are well circumscribed and consist entirely of cysts of variable size; the septa are thin and there are no expansile, solid nodules to alter the rounded contour of the cysts {33673661; 9503503; 2544253}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69446,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CPDNs are composed entirely of septated cysts {168329; 9503503; 2544253}. The cysts are lined with flattened, cuboidal, or hobnail epithelium, or they are denuded. The septa are variably cellular and contain undifferentiated and differentiated mesenchyme (often skeletal muscle, occasionally cartilage or fat), islands of blastema, and nephroblastomatous epithelial elements {9503503}. Focally, the septal elements may protrude into the cysts in microscopic papillary folds. The epithelial components consist mainly of mature and immature tubules and small papillae resembling immature glomeruli {9503503; 2544253}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69447,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69448,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No specific molecular abnormalities have been reported for these tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69449,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> CPDN must lack solid nodules on gross or microscopic examination; septa contain (undifferentiated) mesenchyme, as well as blastemal and immature epithelial elements.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69450,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69451,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 46,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Surgery is almost always curative {17162067; 12778388}. Patients with stage&nbsp;I disease are cured by surgery without adjuvant chemotherapy {12778388}. Rare recurrences have been reported as a complication of incomplete resection {2544253} or tumour rupture {16786584}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:42:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]